  "presentation_summary": [
    "52-year-old woman presented four months after mild RT-PCR-confirmed COVID-19 with gradual shortness of breath, proximal muscle weakness, generalized body aches, and fatigue.",
    "She had MRC 3/5 proximal shoulder and pelvic-girdle weakness with difficulty combing hair, placing objects on shelves, rising from sitting, and using stairs.",
    "Initial vitals were stable and oxygen saturation was 97% on room air; there was no dysphagia, rash, Raynaud phenomenon, joint pain, joint swelling, orthopnea, or chest pain.",
    "Initial labs included CK 2225 U/L, CRP 40.5 mg/dL, WBC 13.0 x10^3/uL, platelets 553 x10^3/uL, ALT 132 U/L, and creatinine 1.1 mg/dL.",
    "EMG, muscle MRI, muscle biopsy, final diagnosis, and treatment response are preserved as confirmatory or non-ranking workup evidence."
  ],
